# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository.
#
# Not cosmetic. CRLF has cost this project real time three times:
#   * gt_pairs.tsv was written in text mode, and a trailing CR made an external
#     join resolve 0 of 7,638,365 rows;
#   * a V7 checkpoint's five artifact digests all looked divergent from another
#     machine's until the bytes were normalised, at which point two matched
#     exactly;
#   * a submission zip built from the Windows checkout carried CRLF on five of
#     twenty-one source files, so it could not be verified byte-for-byte against
#     the revision that produced it.
#
# With this in place a fresh checkout on any platform yields the bytes git stores,
# so digests and packaged files are comparable across machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.npz binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
